     line-number ranges, abbreviated to a single number when a
     range covers only one line, refer to _f_i_l_e_1 and _f_i_l_e_2 respec-
     tively.  The text removed from _f_i_l_e_1 follows, each line
     marked with < , then a --- separator, then the text added
     from _f_i_l_e_2, each line marked with > .

     If either _f_i_l_e_1 or _f_i_l_e_2 is -, the standard input is read
     for it.  If one of the two names a directory, the file com-
